T1  - Management of drug misuse: an 8-year follow-up survey of Scottish GPs.
DO  - https://dx.doi.org/10.3399/bjgp10X514783
A1  - Matheson, Catriona
A1  - Porteous, Terry
A1  - van Teijlingen, Edwin
A1  - Bond, Christine
Y1  - 2010//
N2  - This study repeated a Scotland-wide survey of one-in-four GPs from 2000, to compare findings with 2008. A 60% response was achieved (of 1065). Almost 44% of GPs were treating drug misusers (62% in 2000). Enhanced services were provided by less than half of practices. Seven per cent of responders were only comfortable prescribing below the recommended minimum dose of 60 mg methadone, (33% in 2000). Over 70% offered blood-borne virus screening and 71% were aware of patients using psychostimulants. Recent changes, particularly the new GP contract may have decreased GP involvement in treating drug misusers.
