T1  - Strong opioids for osteoarthritis in primary care?.
DO  - https://dx.doi.org/10.1136/dtb.2009.11.0053
A1  - Anonymous
Y1  - 2009//
N2  - For some patients with osteoarthritis, commonly used drugs taken alone or in combination, offer insufficient pain relief, or are inappropriate. One issue this raises is whether strong opioids might then have a place in treatment. Some GPs may be reluctant to prescribe strong opioids for osteoarthritis. This may be due to concerns about addiction or long-term use of controlled drugs for non-cancer pain. Here we review the evidence on strong opioids as adjunctive treatment in osteoarthritis.
