T1  - Factors associated with the provision of anti-smoking advice in general practice consultations.
A1  - Wynn, Alison
A1  - Coleman, Tim
A1  - Barrett, Stephen
A1  - Wilson, Andrew
Y1  - 2002//
N2  - Guidelines urge general practitioners (GPs) to discuss smoking with patients as frequently as possible. Using data collected before and after consultations, this study confirms that GPs are more likely to discuss smoking in the context of smoking-related problems. Encouraging GPs to make greater use of problem-orientated opportunities to discuss smoking may have more effect on rates of advice giving than urging them to advise all smokers.
